      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nelson sits on the Rock River and once hosted the historic Nelson Rail Bridge, a through‑truss bridge built in 1889 that linked the town to Sterling.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
